<h1>Delete Account – ChessNearby</h1>

<p>
This page explains how users of the <strong>ChessNearby</strong> application
can request deletion of their account and associated personal data.
</p>

<h2>How to request account deletion</h2>

<p>
If you wish to delete your ChessNearby account and all associated data,
please send an email request to:
</p>

<p>
<strong>takate.app@gmail.com</strong>
</p>

<p>
Please include the subject line:
</p>

<p>
<strong>"Account Deletion Request"</strong>
</p>

<p>
To help us identify your account, include the email address or user ID
used to sign in to the application.
</p>

<h2>Data that will be deleted</h2>

<p>
Upon processing your request, the following data will be permanently deleted
from our active systems (Supabase and Firebase):
</p>

<ul>
  <li>User account and authentication records</li>
  <li>Profile information (username, avatar, rating)</li>
  <li>Chat messages and conversation history</li>
  <li>Challenge data created by the user</li>
  <li>Location-related data associated with challenges</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data retention</h2>

<p>
Some information may be retained for a limited period if required for legal,
security, or fraud-prevention purposes. Any retained data will be removed
within a reasonable timeframe, typically within <strong>30 days</strong>.
</p>

<h2>Additional information</h2>

<p>
Uninstalling the application will stop further data collection, but it will
not automatically delete your account or stored data.
</p>

<p>
For more details about how we handle personal information, please review our
<a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.
</p>

